IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc3-disability-payments`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 (housing costs element for renters): paragraphs 13 to 16, the housing cost
-- contributions deducted for non-dependants.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- A non-dependant is identified by paragraph 9 (module uc3-sch4-bedrooms). This module takes the non-dependants as a list and decides, for each, whether
-- paragraph 16 exempts them, and for the renter whether paragraph 15 exempts the renter from any deduction at all. The deduction is taken off the
-- amount that the rest of Part 4 or Part 5 produces (paragraph 14(2)); the element cannot go below nil (paragraph 14(3)).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 14(1): the amount of each housing cost contribution.
-- src:2314 | (1) The amount of each housing cost contribution to be deducted under paragraph 13 is £96.55.
@ref Sch 4 para 14(1) (src:2314)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 14(1) — the amount of each housing cost contribution` MEANS 96.55

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 15(2): the persons whose presence exempts the renter. (a) blind; (b) to (da) in receipt of one of seven payments; (e) entitled to one
-- of six of them but not receiving it. The seven in (b) to (da) are the list of Schedule 3 paragraph 5(3)(b).
-- src:2323 | (2) This sub-paragraph applies to—
-- src:2324 | (a) a person who is ... blind;
-- src:2325 | (b) a person in receipt of the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2326 | (ba) a person in receipt of the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations;
-- src:2327 | (bb) a person in receipt of the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2328 | (c) a person in receipt of attendance allowance;
-- src:2329 | (ca) a person in receipt of pension age disability payment;
-- src:2330 | (d) a person in receipt of the daily living component of personal independence payment;
-- src:2331 | (da) a person in receipt of the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate;
-- src:2332 | (e) a person who is entitled to a payment within paragraph (b) , (bb) , (c) , (ca), (d) or (da) but is not receiving it under, as the case may be—
-- src:2333 | (i) regulation 8 of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2334 | (ii) regulation 6 of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2335 | (iii) regulation 21 of the Social Security (General Benefit) Regulations 1982, ...
-- src:2336 | (iv) regulations under section 86 of the Act (payment of personal independence payment while a person is a hospital in-patient) ...;
-- src:2337 | (v) regulation 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 , ...
-- src:2338 | (vi) regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024 , or
-- src:2339 | (vii) regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025.
@ref Sch 4 para 15(2) (src:2323-2339)
DECLARE `Person to whom paragraph 15(2) may apply` HAS
    `sight certificate`                                                          IS A `Sight certificate`
    payments                                                                     IS A `Disability payments of a person`

-- src:2323 | (2) This sub-paragraph applies to—
-- src:2324 | (a) a person who is ... blind;
-- src:2325 | (b) a person in receipt of the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2326 | (ba) a person in receipt of the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations;
-- src:2327 | (bb) a person in receipt of the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2328 | (c) a person in receipt of attendance allowance;
-- src:2329 | (ca) a person in receipt of pension age disability payment;
-- src:2330 | (d) a person in receipt of the daily living component of personal independence payment;
-- src:2331 | (da) a person in receipt of the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate;
-- src:2332 | (e) a person who is entitled to a payment within paragraph (b) , (bb) , (c) , (ca), (d) or (da) but is not receiving it under, as the case may be—
-- src:2333 | (i) regulation 8 of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2334 | (ii) regulation 6 of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2335 | (iii) regulation 21 of the Social Security (General Benefit) Regulations 1982, ...
-- src:2336 | (iv) regulations under section 86 of the Act (payment of personal independence payment while a person is a hospital in-patient) ...;
-- src:2337 | (v) regulation 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 , ...
-- src:2338 | (vi) regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024 , or
-- src:2339 | (vii) regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025.
@ref Sch 4 para 15(2) (src:2323-2339)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to whom paragraph 15(2) may apply`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` person MEANS
    (`reg 2 — blind` (person's `sight certificate`))
    OR (`Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (person's payments))
    OR (`Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (person's payments))

-- Paragraph 15(1): no deduction for a single renter to whom (2) applies, or for joint renters where at least one of them is such a person.
-- src:2320 | (1) No deduction is to be made under paragraph 13 in the case of—
-- src:2321 | (a) any renter who is a single person to whom sub-paragraph (2) applies; or
-- src:2322 | (b) any joint renter where at least one joint renter is a person to whom sub-paragraph (2) applies.
@ref Sch 4 para 15(1) (src:2320-2322)
DECLARE `Renter who may be exempt from housing cost contributions` HAS
    `claim basis`                                                                IS A `Claim basis`
    `the renter`                                                                 IS A `Person to whom paragraph 15(2) may apply`
    `the other joint renter`                                                     IS A `Person to whom paragraph 15(2) may apply`

-- src:2320 | (1) No deduction is to be made under paragraph 13 in the case of—
-- src:2321 | (a) any renter who is a single person to whom sub-paragraph (2) applies; or
-- src:2322 | (b) any joint renter where at least one joint renter is a person to whom sub-paragraph (2) applies.
@ref Sch 4 para 15(1) (src:2320-2322)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be exempt from housing cost contributions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 15(1) — no deduction is made because of the renter` renter MEANS
    IF (renter's `claim basis`) EQUALS `joint claimants`
    THEN (`Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (renter's `the renter`)) OR (`Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (renter's `the other joint renter`))
    ELSE `Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (renter's `the renter`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 16(2): the non-dependants for whom no deduction is made.
-- src:2342 | (2) This sub-paragraph applies to—
-- src:2343 | (a) a person who is under 21 years old;
-- src:2344 | (b) a person in receipt of state pension credit;
-- src:2345 | (c) a person in receipt of the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2346 | (ca) a person in receipt of the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate;
-- src:2347 | (d) a person in receipt of attendance allowance;
-- src:2348 | (da) a person in receipt of pension age disability payment;
-- src:2349 | (e) a person in receipt of the daily living component of personal independence payment;
-- src:2350 | (ea) a person in receipt of the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate;
-- src:2351 | (f) a person who is entitled to a payment within paragraph (c) , (ca) , (d) , (da), (e) or (ea) but is not receiving it under, as the case may be—
-- src:2352 | (i) regulation 8 of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2353 | (ii) regulation 6 of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2354 | (iii) regulation 21 of the Social Security (General Benefit) Regulations 1982, ...
-- src:2355 | (iv) regulations under section 86 of the Act (payment of personal independence payment while a person is a hospital in-patient) ...;
-- src:2356 | (v) regulation 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 , ...
-- src:2357 | (vi) regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024;, or
-- src:2358 | (vii) regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2359 | (g) a person in receipt of carer's allowance;
-- src:2360 | (ga) a person in receipt of carer support payment;
-- src:2361 | (h) a person who is a prisoner;
-- src:2362 | (i) a person who is responsible for a child under 5 years old.
-- src:2363 | (j) a person who is a member of the armed forces away on operations who—
-- src:2364 | (i) is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters, and
-- src:2365 | (ii) resided with the renter or joint renters immediately before leaving to go on operations and intends to return to reside with the renter or joint renters at the end of the operations.
@ref Sch 4 para 16(2) (src:2342-2365)
DECLARE `Non-dependant who may be exempt from a deduction` HAS
    `age in complete years`                                                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `in receipt of state pension credit`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    payments                                                                                                          IS A `Disability payments of a person`
    `in receipt of carer's allowance`                                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `in receipt of carer support payment`                                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    detention                                                                                                         IS A Detention
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a child"
    `responsible for a child under 5 years old`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of the armed forces away on operations`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `resided with the renter or joint renters immediately before leaving to go on operations`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `intends to return to reside with the renter or joint renters at the end of the operations`                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2363 | (j) a person who is a member of the armed forces away on operations who—
-- src:2364 | (i) is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters, and
-- src:2365 | (ii) resided with the renter or joint renters immediately before leaving to go on operations and intends to return to reside with the renter or joint renters at the end of the operations.
@ref Sch 4 para 16(2)(j) (src:2363-2365)
GIVEN person IS A `Non-dependant who may be exempt from a deduction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 16(2)(j) — a member of the armed forces away on operations` person MEANS
    (person's `a member of the armed forces away on operations`)
    AND (person's `the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters`)
    AND (person's `resided with the renter or joint renters immediately before leaving to go on operations`)
    AND (person's `intends to return to reside with the renter or joint renters at the end of the operations`)

-- src:2342 | (2) This sub-paragraph applies to—
-- src:2343 | (a) a person who is under 21 years old;
-- src:2344 | (b) a person in receipt of state pension credit;
-- src:2345 | (c) a person in receipt of the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2346 | (ca) a person in receipt of the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate;
-- src:2347 | (d) a person in receipt of attendance allowance;
-- src:2348 | (da) a person in receipt of pension age disability payment;
-- src:2349 | (e) a person in receipt of the daily living component of personal independence payment;
-- src:2350 | (ea) a person in receipt of the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate;
-- src:2351 | (f) a person who is entitled to a payment within paragraph (c) , (ca) , (d) , (da), (e) or (ea) but is not receiving it under, as the case may be—
-- src:2352 | (i) regulation 8 of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2353 | (ii) regulation 6 of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2354 | (iii) regulation 21 of the Social Security (General Benefit) Regulations 1982, ...
-- src:2355 | (iv) regulations under section 86 of the Act (payment of personal independence payment while a person is a hospital in-patient) ...;
-- src:2356 | (v) regulation 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 , ...
-- src:2357 | (vi) regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024;, or
-- src:2358 | (vii) regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2359 | (g) a person in receipt of carer's allowance;
-- src:2360 | (ga) a person in receipt of carer support payment;
-- src:2361 | (h) a person who is a prisoner;
-- src:2362 | (i) a person who is responsible for a child under 5 years old.
-- src:2363 | (j) a person who is a member of the armed forces away on operations who—
-- src:2364 | (i) is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters, and
-- src:2365 | (ii) resided with the renter or joint renters immediately before leaving to go on operations and intends to return to reside with the renter or joint renters at the end of the operations.
@ref Sch 4 para 16(2) (src:2342-2365)
GIVEN person IS A `Non-dependant who may be exempt from a deduction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` person MEANS
    (person's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 21)
    OR (person's `in receipt of state pension credit`)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (person's payments))
    OR (`Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (person's payments))
    OR (person's `in receipt of carer's allowance`)
    OR (person's `in receipt of carer support payment`)
    OR (`reg 2 — prisoner` (person's detention))
    OR (person's `responsible for a child under 5 years old`)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 16(2)(j) — a member of the armed forces away on operations` person)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraphs 13 and 14(1): one contribution for each non-dependant in the extended benefit unit, unless paragraph 15 or 16 exempts.
-- src:2310 | (1) In calculating the amount of the housing costs element under Part 4 or 5 of this Schedule, a deduction is to be made in respect of each non-dependant who is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit.
-- src:2311 | (2) Paragraph (1) is subject to paragraphs 15 and 16.
-- src:2312 | (3) Any amount to be deducted under sub-paragraph (1) is referred to in this Schedule as a “housing cost contribution”.
@ref Sch 4 para 13 (src:2310-2312)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be exempt from housing cost contributions`
      nondependants IS A LIST OF `Non-dependant who may be exempt from a deduction`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 13 — the number of housing cost contributions to be deducted` renter nondependants MEANS
    IF `Sch 4 para 15(1) — no deduction is made because of the renter` renter
    THEN 0
    ELSE count (filter (GIVEN person YIELD NOT (`Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` person)) nondependants)

-- src:2310 | (1) In calculating the amount of the housing costs element under Part 4 or 5 of this Schedule, a deduction is to be made in respect of each non-dependant who is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit.
-- src:2311 | (2) Paragraph (1) is subject to paragraphs 15 and 16.
-- src:2312 | (3) Any amount to be deducted under sub-paragraph (1) is referred to in this Schedule as a “housing cost contribution”.
-- src:2313 | 14 Amount of housing cost contributions
-- src:2314 | (1) The amount of each housing cost contribution to be deducted under paragraph 13 is £96.55.
@ref Sch 4 para 13 and para 14(1) (src:2310-2314)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be exempt from housing cost contributions`
      nondependants IS A LIST OF `Non-dependant who may be exempt from a deduction`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 13 — the sum of the housing cost contributions` renter nondependants MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 13 — the number of housing cost contributions to be deducted` renter nondependants) TIMES (`Sch 4 para 14(1) — the amount of each housing cost contribution`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 14(2) and (3): the deductions come last; where they exceed the amount, the amount is reduced to nil, and no further reduction is made from the award.
-- src:2315 | (2) Deductions are not to be made until the amount has been determined which results from all other steps in the calculation required in relation to the renter under Parts 4 and 5 of this Schedule.
-- src:2316 | (3) Where the sum of all the housing cost contributions to be deducted in the renter's case exceeds the amount referred to in sub-paragraph (2)—
-- src:2317 | (a) the amount determined under this Schedule is to be reduced to nil; but
-- src:2318 | (b) no further reduction in respect of housing cost contributions is to be made from the renter's award.
@ref Sch 4 para 14(2) and (3) (src:2315-2318)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      contributions IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 14(2) and (3)(a) — the amount after the housing cost contributions are deducted` amount contributions MEANS
    max 0 (amount MINUS contributions)

-- src:2318 | (b) no further reduction in respect of housing cost contributions is to be made from the renter's award.
@ref Sch 4 para 14(3)(b) (src:2318)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      contributions IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 14(3)(b) — the further reduction of the award for housing cost contributions` amount contributions MEANS 0
